    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25230" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διᾰμάω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to cut through,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χιτῶνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.359
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκὴν παρηΐδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					1023
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ λαιμὸν ἀμῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.374
				</span></i>
			 (tm.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>scrape</i> or <i>clear away,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δακτύλοις δ. χθόνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					709
				</span></i>
			:—also in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαμᾶσθαι τὸν κάχληκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν χιόνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.55.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ψάμμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					3.1.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
